{
  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: Our best result so far is config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) at 52.7% accuracy, showing a modest ~4pp gain over RNA-only (48.5%) and a negligible difference between concat and weighted fusion. The single most important unexplored design dimension is profile setting (single vs. multi), which has not been tested in any completed experiment. Question: config_018 is a clean single-variable extension of config_016—identical model setting, RNA encoder, image encoder, and fusion—changing only the profile setting from single to multi (necessitating avgpool aggregation). This directly tests whether multiprofile + avgpool aggregation improves upon the current best configuration. Why best next experiment: If multiprofile helps, it opens a high-value direction across many downstream configs (different encoders, fusion methods, aggregation strategies). If it does not help, we can efficiently prune the entire multiprofile branch and focus remaining budget on RNA encoder or image encoder choices within singleprofile. This one experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about a major architectural axis while building directly on our strongest evidence."
}

